import json
CO='/home/user/ADHD-learning/hairloss-research/companies/philip-kingsley'
c=json.load(open(CO+'/company.json'))
P={p['id']:p for p in c['products']}
P['p-3combo']['recommendedWhen']='Never offered as served. Its rule was meant for men choosing "Temples and Crown with reduced density" with a visible scalp and no scalp conditions, but it asks for the answer text "Temples & Crown with Reduced Density", which the quiz does not have (code). PHI1304 did not pass in any of the 46 live replays (for example runs/m05, which chose that picture).'
P['p-sku1220']['recommendedWhen']='Every man who passes the shared safety blockers (no pain/burning/crusting/bleeding, no cancer/PSA, depression or trying for a baby, gradual loss already noticed) and has no minoxidil allergy, itching or dandruff, whatever his pattern; also kept with uncontrolled blood pressure and with finasteride allergy (code; live runs/b-men, m25, m31). It is the only thing left, with PHI1221, for Patchy, Extensive or reduced-density loss and for psoriasis, redness or other scalp conditions (runs/m01, m02, m05, m19-m21). Name not found; may be a retired product the server hides.'
P['p-sku1221']['recommendedWhen']='Same safety blockers as PHI1220, plus finasteride allergy, declining finasteride, uncontrolled blood pressure, itching or dandruff (code; live runs/m25, m31). Kept with minoxidil allergy (runs/m30), so it behaves like a finasteride-type product. Name not found; may be retired.'
P['p-scalp-addons-men']['recommendedWhen']='PHI1306 + PHI1309: men with mild or moderate itching or eczema (runs/m15, m18); PHI1306, PHI1307, PHI1309: men with mild dandruff, beside the two Healthy Scalp plans (runs/m17); PHI1306 alone is also added for "Early signs" men under 50 (runs/m03). All code, confirmed in the live page.'
c['engineSummary']=('A rules engine that runs in the browser and is fully visible. Each product SKU has "conditions" (hair-loss picture, density, age, scalp state) that must be true and "blockers" (safety answers) that must all be false; questions are matched by their on-screen label text. '
 'Every SKU that passes is listed in "Recommended" and "Other" groups; if none passes, the person gets the "Choose your consultation type" screen (virtual from £200 or clinic from £345). That is the three-route triage: subscribe (something passes), consultation (everything blocked), or the clinic booking link that skips the quiz. '
 'What decides the route: (1) safety answers block everything (men: sudden or not-yet-noticed loss, pain/burning/crusting/bleeding, cancer or PSA monitoring, depression or anxiety, trying for a baby, severe itching or dandruff, allergy to both actives; women: pregnant or breastfeeding, chemotherapy, patches, band-like or other patterns, psoriasis, redness, acne, other or moderate-to-severe scalp symptoms, minoxidil allergy, oral minoxidil); '
 '(2) the hair-loss picture picks the product family (men: Temples / Temples and Crown / Early signs get minoxidil, oral finasteride and combination plans; Patchy, Extensive and reduced-density pictures keep only two unnamed SKUs; women: shedding gets cosmetic Hair Shedding Drops, other common pictures get the main SKU PHI1749); (3) mild scalp symptoms swap hair-loss plans for "Healthy Scalp" plans; (4) single allergies remove the matching active; men 50+ with Early signs or Temples lose oral finasteride. '
 'Family history, density for the common pictures, onset timing within gradual loss, medicines, other allergies, menopause and HRT change nothing. Women\'s hair type and styling answers only pick a haircare add-on. '
 'All of this was confirmed in 46 live replays by running the site\'s own rule function at the wall; the results screen itself needs an account, and it comes before any result, so nobody learns their route (even a £200+ consultation) until they have registered.')
c['strengths']=[
 'One transparent, simple triage: every product has explicit safety blockers, and anyone who trips one is routed to a paid trichologist consultation rather than refused.',
 'Consultation fallback is a real service with a calendar (virtual or clinic; trichologist or senior trichologist; male or female consultant).',
 'Scalp-first approach: mild scalp symptoms swap hair-loss plans for "Healthy Scalp" plans; severe symptoms go to a consultation; a separate scalp quiz exists.',
 'Women have their own quiz with a shedding route (cosmetic Hair Shedding Drops) and a haircare add-on chosen from hair type, length and styling: a natural upsell.',
 'Strong safety coverage for a short quiz: cancer/PSA, depression with a specific finasteride mood warning, trying for a baby, pregnancy, chemotherapy and oral minoxidil are all screened before any product.',
 'Men must confirm on the start screen that the finasteride and minoxidil products are unlicensed; leaflets say they are made under pharmacist supervision.',
]
c['weaknesses']=[
 'Account wall before any result: name, date of birth, email and password are taken before the person learns whether they get a plan or must pay £200-£345 for a consultation. The wall screen is identical for both routes (43 live variants checked).',
 'Configuration errors in the served rules: the blood-pressure blocker has a leading space, so men who tick uncontrolled low or high blood pressure are still offered minoxidil 5% and the combination plans (live runs/m25); the 3% Combination Plan can never be offered; PHI1230 and PHI1770-1772 can never fire; label typos ("curerrently", "redness??").',
 'Women: sudden loss with a widening parting is not escalated (live runs/w09), while the same change with overall thinning is (runs/w10); menopause and HRT answers are unused; no finasteride product is ever offered to women online.',
 'Thin clinical screen: no under-18 answer (age bands start at 18; the women\'s quiz asks no age at all), one tick-box for blood pressure, no heart, kidney, liver or sexual side-effect questions; medicines and allergies are free text that no rule reads.',
 'Men with Patchy, Extensive or reduced-density loss, or psoriasis/redness, are not routed to a consultation in the rules; they keep two unnamed SKUs (PHI1220, PHI1221). Whether these are still sold decides what they see.',
 'Family history and hair density do not change the offer for the common male pictures, and the women\'s "how noticeable" follow-ups are never used: questions that look diagnostic are decoration.',
 'Mixed messages: the men\'s page says "FULLY LICENSED" while leaflets say unlicensed; prices differ between pages (oral finasteride £40 vs £42; virtual consultation from £150 vs from £200).',
 'Who prescribes is not stated anywhere public (trichologists are not prescribers; leaflets only say "pharmacist supervision").',
]
c['opportunities']=[
 'Show the route (plan or consultation, and its price) before asking for an account. PK makes people register before they find out they owe £200+.',
 'Offer a cheaper middle route for the people PK sends to a £200-£345 consultation (sudden shedding, mild-to-moderate scalp symptoms, patchy loss): a prescriber review with photos at a fixed lower price.',
 'A prescriber-led women\'s offer: PK sells women only a minoxidil-type drop or cosmetic shedding drops online; no oral minoxidil, spironolactone or topical finasteride for post-menopausal women, and menopause answers are ignored.',
 'Use the answers PK collects but ignores (family history, density, menopause, medicines) to personalise strength and expectations: an easy way to look more clinical.',
 'Clear licensing and prescriber information, and a blood-pressure and heart screen that actually works, as trust signals against a premium brand whose rules contain visible mistakes.',
]
c['limitations']=[
 'The results screen is behind the account wall, so the plan list as rendered by the server, its order, the default choice and the 1/2/3-month plan prices were not seen. Product effects come from the site\'s own rule function run in the live page at the wall (46 replays) and from the served rule file; the server could still hide SKUs or show something different after registration.',
 'The server may hide retired SKUs (for example PHI1220/PHI1221). If so, Patchy/Extensive men and men with psoriasis, redness or other scalp conditions would reach the consultation screen instead. Cannot be tested without an account. A search of the hairloss store for SKU codes returns nothing (even for known SKUs), so it could not settle this.',
 'Not replayed live (effects taken from the served rules only): men-q1 Temples and Crown with reduced density beyond one picture, men-q2a "slightly visible" and "extensive", men-q4 "It\'s not started yet", men-q5 "Don\'t know", men-q6 "18 to 29" and "40 to 49", men-q7a Acne, moderate itching/dandruff/redness, severe eczema, men-q8 Crusting and Bleeding, men-q9 combinations; women thinning at temples, band-like recession, something else, women-q4 "a few months", dandruff, redness, eczema and other symptoms, women-q6 to q9 (haircare add-on choices), women-q11a other allergy, women-q12a medical condition; the scalp quiz beyond Q1/Q2. Every live replay matched the code reading exactly, so these are high-confidence code findings.',
 'Some SKUs could not be named (PHI1220, PHI1221, PHI1306, PHI1307, PHI1309, PHI1749, women\'s add-ons, scalp products). Contents of the combination plans are partly inferred from their names.',
 'Who prescribes and which pharmacy compounds and dispenses was not found in public pages. Questions after registration (if any), photo upload and the prescriber\'s review were not seen.',
]
a=c['access']
a['coverageNote']=('Stage 1 walked all three quizzes to the account wall and saved the full served quiz definition. Stage 2 replayed the three baselines and 43 one-change variants (46 replays, runs/b-* , m*, w*, s01), each to the wall. At the wall the site\'s own client function window.quiz.checkProductAvailability() was run read-only in the live page (scratch/walk-eval.js), which returns the SKUs the results page would list; it matched the Python port of the rules in all 46 runs, so the served rules have not changed. '
 'Follow-up questions (show-ifs) were seen live; no answer produced a warning screen, stop screen or different wall before registration. Results screens themselves were not seen (account wall).')
json.dump(c,open(CO+'/company.json','w'),indent=1,ensure_ascii=False)
